  "limitations": [
    "Remediation of the attempt-01 findings (RF01-RF04, the T06 evidence gap and the optional validator suggestion) is documented in docs/planning/reviews/C02/remediation-attempt-01.md with the tests and mutation probes that guard each change.",
    "D027 (docs/planning/decisions.md) replaces the ec6230d2 SDK source pin with the published crates.io scm-sdk =0.1.0 (sha256 6d555d95..., from 4f65dc48) on owner direction. The package's own 164 unit tests run natively from the checksum-verified .crate via xtask sdk-test (C02/host/3). Live endpoint qualification is C25; the scan operation and its UI are C03. C02 exercises the shared operation lifecycle through a test-fixtures-only admission hook (AuthorityHandle::admit_fixture_operation).",
    "Native acceptance uses the fixture build, whose credentials live in a dedicated fixture test keychain under a fixture namespace (DESIGN); the production login-keychain path is covered by keychain_access (read-only availability on macOS 27) and, signed, in C26. A trial run showed that a lock made by another process (security lock-keychain) is not observed by the running fixture app on macOS 27, so C02-N07 locks through the app's own keychain reference via fixture-only menu items; superseded and trial runs with their causes are retained under docs/planning/evidence/C02/native-trial/.",
    "System proxy mode is qualified through the proxy environment (HTTPS_PROXY changed between admissions); the macOS SCDynamicStore proxy settings were not changed on this host. reqwest reads only the macOS HTTP/HTTPS proxy entries (no PAC, auto-discovery or bypass list). C02 provides no operator UI for the transport policy (Direct default); C15 adds it.",
    "Endpoint overrides are reviewed in the presentation (stored native review, confirm with the same context and review) and never carry an existing key to the new destination: the key must be re-entered. A native AppKit confirmation sheet is the C09 mechanism for operator Apply and is not used here.",
    "Profile import supports the v2 profile document and the airs-cli tenant registry; importing from v1's own data store is C23. That a referenced credential file is never opened is shown by core tests and the absent file in native acceptance, not by file-system tracing. The FileStore directory-sync failure is exercised by fault injection (StoreFault, fixture builds only), not by a real failing filesystem."
  ],
